  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is for RNA multiprofile with avgpool, where PCA reaches 0.591 accuracy and 0.573 F1, outperforming transformer aggregation and scGPT avgpool; image-only models are weak. The main remaining uncertainty is whether a learned RNA representation such as scvi_n200 can improve on PCA in this best-known setting. config_005 changes only the RNA encoder while keeping multiprofile and avgpool fixed, cleanly isolating the representation effect. Under a limited budget, this is more informative than moving directly to multimodal fusion because it clarifies the best RNA backbone first and avoids confounding encoder, profile, aggregation, and fusion choices."
